.TH AEGIS 1 "October 2026" "Aegis 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aegis \- Linux security auditing and safe-hardening framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aegis
[--root PATH] COMMAND [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Aegis audits Linux security controls, inventories attack surface, applies selected managed remediations transactionally, and records rollback metadata.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B audit
Run security checks. Supports --profile, --module, --tag, --json, --html, --sarif, --fail-on and optional HMAC signing. GitHub Code Scanning requires an explicit SARIF source-location map.
.TP
.B profiles
List built-in host role profiles.
.TP
.B baseline create|compare
Capture or compare reviewed listening-socket and SUID/SGID state. Creating an existing baseline requires --force; signed baselines require --verify-key when compared.
.TP
.B policy validate|migrate|example
Work with versioned host policy.
.TP
.B integrity keygen|sign|verify
Protect reports/baselines with HMAC-SHA256 metadata.
.TP
.B preflight / fix / rollback
Plan, validate, apply and reverse supported hardening changes.
.SH SECURITY
Aegis is conservative by design. Review policy, keep a second administrative session for SSH changes, and test on disposable systems before production use.
.SH FILES
/etc/aegis/policy.json, /var/lib/aegis/backups/, /var/log/aegis/events.jsonl
